---
// Migrated verbatim from public/topics/software-concepts/lessons/0001-sql-foundations.html (URL unchanged: builds to 0001-sql-foundations.html).
// Body is is:raw: braces/inline scripts/JSON blocks pass through untouched.
import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "SQL básico — selecionar, combinar e resumir";
const titleEn = "Basic SQL — select, join, and aggregate";
const titleFallback = "Basic SQL";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/concepts.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/reading-ui.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/concepts.js\" defer></script>",
];

---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow"
          >⬡ SQL · <span data-lang="pt">fundamentos</span
          ><span data-lang="en">foundations</span></span
        >
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">Pergunte aos dados.</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Ask the data.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Em 15 minutos: escolher colunas, filtrar linhas, combinar tabelas e
            transformar muitas linhas em um resumo.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >In 15 minutes: choose columns, filter rows, combine tables, and
            turn many rows into a summary.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>
      <nav class="concept-nav">
        <a href="0001-sql-foundations.html">SQL</a
        ><a href="0002-oauth-flow.html">OAuth →</a
        ><a href="0003-sql-sandbox.html">⌨ Sandbox</a
        ><a href="../reference/software-concepts-cheatsheet.html"
          ><span data-lang="pt">Folha rápida</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Cheat sheet</span></a
        ><a href="../../../index.html">Hub</a>
      </nav>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span><span data-lang="pt">O modelo mental</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The mental model</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Uma consulta SQL é um pipeline:
          <strong
            >comece pelas linhas, reduza, agrupe e finalmente apresente</strong
          >. A ordem escrita não é exatamente a ordem mental de execução.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >An SQL query is a pipeline:
          <strong
            >start with rows, reduce them, group them, then present them</strong
          >. Written order is not exactly the mental execution order.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="pipeline" aria-label="SQL pipeline">
        <div class="pipe">
          <code>FROM/JOIN</code><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">obter linhas</span
            ><span data-lang="en">get rows</span></small
          >
        </div>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <div class="pipe">
          <code>WHERE</code><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">filtrar</span
            ><span data-lang="en">filter</span></small
          >
        </div>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <div class="pipe">
          <code>GROUP BY</code><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">agrupar</span
            ><span data-lang="en">group</span></small
          >
        </div>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <div class="pipe">
          <code>SELECT</code><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">mostrar</span
            ><span data-lang="en">project</span></small
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mental-model">
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>SELECT</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Quais colunas quero ver?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Which columns do I want?</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>FROM</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">De quais tabelas vêm?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Which tables supply them?</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>WHERE</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Quais linhas sobrevivem?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Which rows survive?</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span><code>SELECT</code> + <code>WHERE</code>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >O <code>SELECT</code> define a saída; <code>WHERE</code> elimina
          linhas que não atendem à condição.
          <strong>SQL descreve o resultado desejado</strong>; o banco decide
          como buscá-lo.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><code>SELECT</code> defines the output; <code>WHERE</code> removes
          rows that fail the condition.
          <strong>SQL describes the desired result</strong>; the database
          decides how to retrieve it.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="code-stage">
        <pre><code><span style="color:#c4b5fd">SELECT</span> id, customer_id, total
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">FROM</span> orders
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">WHERE</span> status = <span style="color:#5eead4">'paid'</span> <span style="color:#c4b5fd">AND</span> total &gt; 100
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">ORDER BY</span> total <span style="color:#c4b5fd">DESC</span>;</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>id</th>
              <th>customer_id</th>
              <th>total</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>104</td>
              <td>2</td>
              <td>240</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>101</td>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>120</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="cite-line">
        <span data-lang="pt">Fonte primária:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Primary source:</span>
        <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/tutorial-select.html"
          >PostgreSQL — Querying a Table</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span><code>JOIN</code>:
        <span data-lang="pt">reconecte relações</span
        ><span data-lang="en">reconnect relationships</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Normalmente guardamos clientes e pedidos separadamente. O
          <code>JOIN ... ON</code> diz
          <strong>qual chave conecta uma linha à outra</strong>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >We normally store customers and orders separately.
          <code>JOIN ... ON</code> says
          <strong>which key connects one row to another</strong>.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="schema">
        <div class="db-table">
          <b>customers</b>
          <div class="db-row"><span>id</span><span>name</span></div>
          <div class="db-row match"><span>1</span><span>Ana</span></div>
          <div class="db-row"><span>2</span><span>Ben</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="join-link">⟷</div>
        <div class="db-table">
          <b>orders</b>
          <div class="db-row"><span>customer_id</span><span>total</span></div>
          <div class="db-row match"><span>1</span><span>120</span></div>
          <div class="db-row"><span>1</span><span>80</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="code-stage">
        <pre><code><span style="color:#c4b5fd">SELECT</span> c.name, o.total
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">FROM</span> customers c
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">JOIN</span> orders o <span style="color:#c4b5fd">ON</span> o.customer_id = c.id;</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="security-pair">
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>INNER JOIN</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Somente pares que têm correspondência.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Only pairs that have a match.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>LEFT JOIN</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Todas as linhas da esquerda; sem par vira
              <code>NULL</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Every left row; a missing match becomes <code>NULL</code>.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cite-line">
        <span data-lang="pt">Fonte primária:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Primary source:</span>
        <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/tutorial-join.html"
          >PostgreSQL — Joins Between Tables</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Agregação: muitas linhas → uma resposta</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Aggregation: many rows → one answer</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><code>COUNT</code>, <code>SUM</code>, <code>AVG</code>,
          <code>MIN</code> e <code>MAX</code> resumem linhas.
          <code>GROUP BY</code> cria um balde por valor:
          <strong>uma linha de saída por grupo</strong>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><code>COUNT</code>, <code>SUM</code>, <code>AVG</code>,
          <code>MIN</code> and <code>MAX</code> summarize rows.
          <code>GROUP BY</code> creates one bucket per value:
          <strong>one output row per group</strong>.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="code-stage">
        <pre><code><span style="color:#c4b5fd">SELECT</span> status,
       <span style="color:#5eead4">COUNT</span>(*) <span style="color:#c4b5fd">AS</span> orders,
       <span style="color:#5eead4">SUM</span>(total) <span style="color:#c4b5fd">AS</span> revenue
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">FROM</span> orders
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">WHERE</span> created_at &gt;= <span style="color:#5eead4">'2026-08-01'</span>
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">GROUP BY</span> status
<span style="color:#c4b5fd">HAVING</span> <span style="color:#5eead4">COUNT</span>(*) &gt; 1;</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>status</th>
              <th>orders</th>
              <th>revenue</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>paid</td>
              <td>3</td>
              <td>440</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>pending</td>
              <td>2</td>
              <td>95</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="callout key">
        <p>
          <strong>WHERE vs HAVING:</strong> <code>WHERE</code>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >filtra linhas antes de agrupar; <code>HAVING</code> filtra grupos
            depois de agregar.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >filters rows before grouping; <code>HAVING</code> filters groups
            after aggregation.</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">5</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Teste de recuperação</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Retrieval check</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="playground" data-sql-quiz data-answer="where">
        <label for="sql-answer"
          ><span data-lang="pt"
            >Você quer receita por status, mas apenas para pedidos de agosto.
            Onde filtra a data?</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >You want revenue by status, but only for August orders. Where do
            you filter the date?</span
          ></label
        ><br /><select id="sql-answer">
          <option value="">—</option>
          <option value="select">SELECT</option>
          <option value="where">WHERE</option>
          <option value="having">HAVING</option></select
        ><button type="button">
          <span data-lang="pt">Verificar</span><span data-lang="en">Check</span>
        </button>
        <div class="result" aria-live="polite">
          <span data-lang="pt">Escolha sem olhar acima.</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Choose without looking above.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span data-lang="pt">Desafio: explique esta consulta em voz alta</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Challenge: explain this query aloud</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Use a ordem: “parte de orders → mantém agosto → cria um grupo por
            status → calcula contagem e soma → mantém grupos com mais de um
            pedido → mostra o resultado”.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Use this order: “start with orders → keep August → make one group
            per status → calculate count and sum → keep groups with more than
            one order → show the result”.</span
          >
        </p>
      </details>
      <div class="callout info">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Dúvida ou quer praticar outra consulta?
            <strong
              >Pergunte ao agente e descreva o resultado desejado antes da
              sintaxe.</strong
            ></span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Confused or want another query?
            <strong
              >Ask the agent and describe the desired result before the
              syntax.</strong
            ></span
          >
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="cite-line">
        <span data-lang="pt">Leitura recomendada:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Recommended reading:</span>
        <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/tutorial-agg.html"
          >PostgreSQL — Aggregate Functions</a
        >.
        <a href="0002-oauth-flow.html"
          ><span data-lang="pt">Próxima lição: OAuth →</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Next lesson: OAuth →</span></a
        >
      </p>
    </article>
  </Fragment>
</Lesson>
